      <div>
        <p><strong>The wheat bag helps — for ten minutes.</strong> Then it's cold, and you're back at the microwave for the fourth time tonight.</p>
        <p><strong>The pills work — until they wear off.</strong> And you'd rather not live on them anyway.</p>
        <p><strong>The physio helps — for a few days.</strong> Then the stiffness creeps back, £50 poorer every visit, next appointment three weeks away.</p>
        <p>None of these failed because your joints are "too far gone." They failed because every one of them gives the joint a <strong>moment</strong> of relief — and a stiff knee, shoulder or elbow doesn't need a moment. It needs relief it can count on, every single day.</p>
        <blockquote class="pull">"I have arthritis in both knees and by the afternoon they feel tight n swollen. I pop this on for 20 mins and it legit loosens everything up."
