<!-- 6 ▸ BELIEF 2 · THE STIFFNESS LOOP -->
<section id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center"><span class="eyebrow">Why relief never lasted</span></div>
    <h2>Stiff joints get stuck in <em>a loop.</em></h2>
    <p class="lede">Knees, shoulders and elbows all sit close to the surface with little muscle around them to keep warm. So when one hurts, the same cycle starts — and quick fixes only pause it.</p>
    <div class="split">
      <figure class="fig">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 440 360" role="img" aria-label="The stiffness loop: a joint that hurts leads to moving less, moving less drops circulation, low circulation stiffens the joint, and a stiffer joint brings more pain — a cycle that repeats.">
          <!-- one unbroken ring: the point is that the cycle never stops.
               Direction is carried by light chevrons, and the four stages are
               marked by dots, so nothing reads as a stray shape. -->
          <circle cx="220" cy="180" r="92" fill="none" stroke="#eee1d5" stroke-width="5"/>
          <g fill="#c8500f">
            <circle cx="220.0" cy="88.0" r="6.5"/>
            <circle cx="312.0" cy="180.0" r="6.5"/>
            <circle cx="220.0" cy="272.0" r="6.5"/>
            <circle cx="128.0" cy="180.0" r="6.5"/>
          </g>
          <g fill="none" stroke="#c8500f" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <polyline points="285.1,105.8 289.7,119.5 275.9,114.9"/>
            <polyline points="294.2,245.1 280.5,249.7 285.1,235.9"/>
